  "question": {
    "text": "$\\int_{-a}^{4}\\left(x^{8}-x^{4}+x^{2}+1\\right) d x=2 \\int_{0}^{4}\\left(x^{8}-x^{4}+x^{2}+1\\right) d x$ then $a=$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "3",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "4",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "6",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "8",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "If $\\mathrm{f}(x)$ is an even function then\r\n\r\n$\\int_{-a}^{a} f(x) d x=2 \\int_{0}^{a} f(x) d x$\r\n\r\nHere $\\mathrm{f}(x)=x^{8}-x^{4}+x^{2}+1$ is an even function, therefore $a=4$."
  }
}